-- title:
--   Affine Drinfeld chart at a supersingular place of X_H(q²M')
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q\ge 5$ and $M'\ge 1$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A$. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places (rational, affine geometric, with the value of the geometric $j$-generator in the supersingular $j$-set for $q$); assume $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'\le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$. Let $R_0$ be a constant reduction of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ along $A$ with values in that residue function field, i.e. a valuation subring with a surjective residue map of kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$, with orders and with degrees of places, and assume $R_0$ reduces coefficientwise: every Laurent series with coefficients in $A$ lying in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ is $R_0$-integral with residue the coefficientwise reduction. Let $\pi\in A$ satisfy $\pi^{q^2-1}=q$, let $\zeta$ be a primitive $q$th root of unity, and let $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}$, indexed by $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb F_q)$, and $O^{\mathrm{ss}}$, indexed by $W$, be families of valuation subrings of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ subject to: $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ consists of the $f$ whose expansion is a quotient $x/y$ of Laurent series over $A$ with $y$ of nonzero reduction; each $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ is the pullback of $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ along $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ for some $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ carrying $\infty$ to $\ell$ modulo $q$; $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ injective and permuted by all $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; each $O^{\mathrm{ss}}(s)$ meets $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in $A$, is fixed by all those automorphisms, contains an element $t$ with $t-a$ a unit for every $a\in A$, and dominates $R_0$ over the place $s$ in the sense that an $R_0$-integral $f$ with nonnegative order wherever $j$ has nonnegative order, whose residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, has image in $O^{\mathrm{ss}}(s)$, with $f-a$ in the maximal ideal whenever the residue of $a\in A$ is the value of the residue of $f$ at $s$. Let further $K_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ be a subfield with $\overline{\mathbb Q}/K_0$ algebraic and $\pi\in K_0$; let $A_0$ be a henselian discrete valuation domain with an injective local homomorphism $\iota:A_0\to A$ whose image is $A\cap K_0$, with $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ generated by the residues of $\iota$, and with uniformiser $\varpi_0$ satisfying $\iota(\varpi_0)=\pi$; let $F_0$ be the subfield of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ of elements all of whose Laurent coefficients lie in $K_0$, an $A_0$-algebra via $\iota$, containing the image $\hat\jmath$ of $j$. Then for each $s\in W$ there is an $A_0$-subalgebra $B\subseteq F_0$ which is finitely generated, integrally closed in $F_0$, has $F_0$ as its field of fractions, has every non-maximal prime containing $\varpi_0 B$ minimal over $\varpi_0B$, has $B_{\mathfrak p}$ a valuation subring of $F_0$ for every nonzero prime $\mathfrak p$ not containing $\varpi_0 B$, contains $\hat\jmath$, satisfies $B\subseteq O^{\mathrm{ss}}(s)$, admits a prime $\mathfrak q_0$ with $O^{\mathrm{ss}}(s)\cap F_0=B_{\mathfrak q_0}$ and $\mathfrak q_0$ the only minimal prime over $\varpi_0B$, is contained in no $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ and in no $O^{\mathrm{ss}}(s')$ with $s'\ne s$, is formally smooth over $A_0$, and is such that any finite set of valuation subrings $V$ of $F_0$ with $V\subseteq O^{\mathrm{ss}}(s)$ properly, and $B\not\subseteq V$, has at most $q+1$ members.
--
--   This produces the affine Drinfeld chart of the descended semistable model of the full-level modular curve at a chosen supersingular point $s$: a normal finitely generated $A_0$-algebra whose localisation at the unique minimal prime over the uniformiser recovers the Drinfeld ring $O^{\mathrm{ss}}(s)$, which meets none of the Igusa rings and no other supersingular ring, is formally smooth over the base, and has at most $q+1$ missing end places, the crossings with the Igusa components. It feeds the construction of the local ring of the Drinfeld chart in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_drinfeldChart_localRing_eq_localization_formallySmooth_of_normalModel_gen_j`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_drinfeldChart_localRing_eq_localization_formallySmooth_of_normalModel_gen_j).
